  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b8c5f8bea1b438d4687ad9b712e77c3e, type: 3}
  m_Name: Level 1-2 Starting Cutscene
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CutsceneData
  line:
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 0}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: "When I first woke up as a baby, I found myself in a village. I felt
      the sun and heard the voices of my parents. After that, I don\u2019t remember
      much from my baby days."
    isLeftSide: 0
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 0}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: I had nine sisters and a brother. Our father was a model parent. He
      gave us the education that was suitable in a family that was neither rich nor
      poor. He was creative and careful with saving money, which allowed him to build
      two houses. One of the two became the house that I lived in with a nipa hut
      nearby, shaded with banana trees, where I had fond memories of.
    isLeftSide: 0
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 0}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: When I was four years of age, my little sister Concha died, and for
      the first time I cried because of love and regret. Until then I had shed tears
      only for my own mistakes, which my loving, wise mother knew how to correct.
    isLeftSide: 0
  - speakerName: Jose Rizal
    speakerType: 0
    hero: {fileID: 0}
    enemy: {fileID: 0}
    Dialogue: Ah... those memories give me grief.
    isLeftSide: 0
